    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386-a1">

                <pb facs="0587" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg499"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 272.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commodore Ramsey to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Replying to your letter of the 16th
                    instant, I have the honor to inform you that Rear-Admiral A. E. K. Benham, U. S.
                    Navy, has been ordered to proceed to Cadiz, Spain, with the United States
                    flagship <hi rendition="#italic">Newark</hi>, by the 8th of October next, and to
                    accompany the Queen Regent of Spain when she leaves that port for Huelva to
                    dedicate the Columbus monument at that city.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M. Ramsey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
